  "run_status": "ok",
  "summary": "Most headline figures reconcile: the pilot funnel (70 → 36 duplicates → 34), the 5/8/21 coding split, Tables 3–4 (33 of 34 = 97%), Table 6 date-precision sums (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the 18+26 = 44 ceremony split, the Table 8 shares and totals (266,625 + 433,954 = 700,579), and the Figure 2 and 4 labels versus the text. Five issues need correction or clarification. (1) The \"about 6 percent\" yield counts 2 distinct openings against 34 articles, although 5 of those articles (14.7%) concern the two openings. (2) Footnote 3 says both human coders coded the Stord article not relevant, but Table 3 and Section 4.1 make it the one article where the coders disagree. (3) The 96-article / 44-project reconciliation in Section 6 cannot be verified because overlap between the pilot and rounds 2–4 is not stated. (4) The count of \"only two actual openings\" sits beside a Table 2 footnote saying the Grettefoss bridge opened on 3 November. (5) The 2024 gap is described as Q1 only in the text but as January–April in the data note. Parser-quality warnings were respected: table values were read from the page text rather than the structured table CSV/markdown, and Figure 3 was checked from the retained crop.",
